00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:53,040
and without using conventional pain medications.

71
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,640
To understand how Dr. Cox's natural protocol

72
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,520
is helping people across America,

73
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,040
even in decade-long bone-on-bone cases

74
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:02,120
and seniors confined to wheelchairs,

75
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,400
move freely and live without pain.

76
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,680
We invited Dr. Sanjay Gupta, renowned neurosurgeon

77
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,080
and CNN's chief medical correspondent,

78
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:13,520
who traveled to Wyoming to interview Dr. Paul Cox personally

79
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,600
and answer two critical questions.

80
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,160
What is this natural protocol

81
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:18,680
that's reversing joint damage

82
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,440
and restoring pain-free movement?

83
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,800
Even in severe bone-on-bone cases.

84
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,080
And how exactly are people using it at home,

85
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,600
step-by-step, to walk, climb stairs

86
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,240
and move through the day without pain

87
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,640
in just a couple of weeks?

88
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,840
When we began investigating chronic back,

89
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,920
knee and hip pain, something didn't make sense.

90
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,800
For 50 years, medicine told us

91
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:41,960
it was simply wear and tear, age, genetics.

92
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,320
But when we examined the data more closely,

93
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,160
it became clear that wasn't the whole story.

94
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:50,040
That trail led us to a small nonprofit laboratory

95
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:51,440
in the mountains of Wyoming,

96
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:54,680
where Dr. Paul Cox has been studying pain biology

97
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,880
and joint aging for years.

98
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,520
The visible damage, worn-down cartilage,

99
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:02,440
bone grinding on bone, that's not the real problem.

100
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:03,920
In fact, that's a symptom.

101
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:05,680
It's like coughing during a cold.

102
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,200
You don't treat the cough alone.

103
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,440
You treat the cold so the cough goes away.

104
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:12,320
I'll be honest, as a physician, I was skeptical at first.

105
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:15,640
Dr. Cox didn't just discover how to stop joint damage.

106
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:18,000
What we saw, again and again,

107
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,880
was the joint rebuilding itself.

108
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:23,120
Worn bones rebuilding, cartilage growing back,

109
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:27,520
synovial fluid refilling, joints gliding smoothly again.

110
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:29,900
Just like a cut on your skin closes,

111
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,680
just like a broken bone heals over time.

112
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,920
The joint structure was rebuilding itself,

113
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:38,280
day after day, without bone-on-bone grinding,

114
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,640
without stiffness, without pain.

115
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:42,080
And this discovery didn't come

116
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,860
from a traditional orthopedist,

117
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:46,600
but from a Harvard-trained ethnobotanist.

118
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,640
Ethnobotanist, what exactly does that mean?

119
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,660
I'm a cure hunter.

120
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,720
I was trained to live among indigenous peoples

121
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,780
and decode how they use herbs, plants, and natural foods

122
00:04:54,780 --> 00:04:56,940
to protect and cure themselves from disease.

123
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:59,060
The logical path is to look at extremes,

124
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:02,400
places where pain is rare, and places where it's everywhere.

125
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,740
The difference between them reveals

126
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,460
what's actually causing the pain.

127
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,860
When Dr. Cox began following this pattern,

128
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:09,740
it led him somewhere unexpected,

129
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:12,540
a small island in the Pacific called Guam.

130
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:14,020
In Guam, what did you find there?

131
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:15,460
It was devastating.

132
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,300
Nearly one out of every four adults

133
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:19,180
could barely walk without support.

134
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:22,740
Knees grinding bone-on-bone, hips locking mid-step,

135
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:24,860
spines collapsing before 60,

136
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:27,580
every family had someone on a cane, a walker,

137
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:30,300
a wheelchair, or waiting for joint replacement.

138
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,620
That wasn't normal aging.

139
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,180
Something was wrong.

140
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:36,300
Rates of severe arthritis and crippling back pain

141
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,740
were dozens of times higher than anywhere else.

142
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:40,020
Age couldn't explain it.

143
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,740
Genetics couldn't explain it either.

144
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:45,700
So Dr. Paul Cox asked one question, what changed?

145
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:47,620
An industrial plant was built right next

146
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:50,060
to the community's main drinking water source.

147
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:54,900
And after that, year after year, joint pain cases surged.

148
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,180
First, the grandparents, then the parents,

149
00:05:57,180 --> 00:06:00,100
then people in their 40s, then even their 30s.

150
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:01,900
That's when we tested the water.

151
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:05,060
And what we found was alarming, cadmium chloride,

152
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:07,200
a highly inflammatory toxin,

153
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,660
at levels I had never seen in my career.

154
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,500
At first, I assumed it was just a local

155
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:12,900
water contamination issue,

156
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,020
but as I read your full research,

157
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,540
I realized something far more disturbing.

158
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:21,100
This wasn't just Guam, cadmium chloride is everywhere.

159
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:21,940
Exactly.

160
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,100
And here's the tricky part.

161
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:26,100
In Guam, cadmium chloride levels were so high

162
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:27,380
they were easy to detect.

163
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:28,640
But in smaller amounts,

164
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:31,320
it slips past standard safety tests.

165
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:33,860
In fact, only a few labs in the entire U.S.

166
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:35,860
can properly measure it.

167
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:37,740
At Harvard, we ran advanced tests

168
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,520
capable of finding even small amounts of cadmium chloride.

169
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,220
And what we found shocked us.

170
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:43,780
Cadmium chloride was present

171
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,940
in nearly every kitchen across America.

172
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:47,940
There is no way to fully escape it.

173
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:50,200
It's in pesticide sprayed on crops.

174
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:53,060
It's in factory waste seeping into soil and rivers.

175
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,340
It's in the packaging your groceries come in.

176
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:57,420
It's in the water from your kitchen tap

177
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,220
and inside bottled water.

178
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:01,180
Even in everyday fruits like apples,

179
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:02,740
strawberries and blueberries,

180
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:04,660
not at Guam's extreme levels,

181
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:07,580
but high enough enough to build up inside the body,

182
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:08,660
enough to inflame,

183
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:11,580
enough to quietly damage joints over time.

184
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,340
But you found a solution for this, right?

185
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,220
A natural one?

186
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:15,060
Not me.

187
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,340
The answer was already there.

188
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:18,180
We just had to look in the right place.

189
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,340
After years of studying

190
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:22,020
how cadmium chloride damages the joints,

191
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:25,100
we discovered something medicine had overlooked for decades.

192
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,580
The solution for chronic pain

193
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:28,260
wasn't a new drug or surgery.

194
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:29,100
The truth is,

195
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,620
it already existed in nature this whole time.

196
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:34,380
It's in two natural compounds that work together.

197
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:35,820
So how do these natural compounds

198
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:38,140
actually repair the damage inside the joints?

199
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:39,380
It's actually simple.

200
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:42,140
One helps the body clear out cadmium chloride.

201
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:44,660
The other helps damaged joints rebuild.

202
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:47,020
And this is where most treatments fail,

203
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:49,220
because in the knees, hips and spine,

204
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,660
the ends of the bones are covered

205
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:52,900
by a protective layer called cartilage

206
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:55,340
and surrounded by a slippery natural lubricant

207
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:56,860
called synovial fluid.

208
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:58,740
Together, they prevent your bones

209
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:00,260
from rubbing against each other

210
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:03,100
every time you stand, walk or bend.

211
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,940
And this is where the pain begins.

212
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:07,460
Cadmium chloride slowly eats away cartilage,

213
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,740
the smooth cushion protecting the joints.

214
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:12,340
At the same time, it dries up synovial fluid,

215
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:14,820
the natural lubricant inside the joints.

216
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:16,620
So instead of moving smoothly,

217
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:20,020
the bones begin to grind against each other day after day

218
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:22,940
that grinding strips the joint down to bare bone

219
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:24,460
until even a small movement

220
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:27,580
causes a sudden knife twist of pain out of nowhere.

221
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:29,740
Then it happens again and again

222
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:31,220
to the point where standing up

223
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,260
becomes something to think about first.

224
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,420
And little by little,

225
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:36,740
independence starts slipping away.

226
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:38,380
So these two natural compounds,

227
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:41,060
how do they actually reverse what you just described?

228
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:43,100
And what exactly are these compounds?

229
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:44,620
Where did you find them?

230
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,180
I didn't start in a laboratory.

231
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:48,620
I started by looking at places where we would expect

232
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:51,180
to see the same level of chronic pain as Guam.

233
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,420
But then I found regions where pain was rare

234
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:55,180
and that raised a critical question.

235
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:56,820
What are they doing differently?

236
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:59,220
My first expedition took me to rural India.

237
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:01,620
There I met men and women in their 60s and 70s

238
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:03,420
still working the fields every day.

239
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:05,340
They harvest under the sun for hours.

240
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:06,780
They lift baskets of crops.

241
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,260
They carry water by hand.

242
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:09,940
They squat again and again.

243
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:12,500
Their joints simply did not match their age.

244
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,820
Even more surprising, in these villages,

245
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:17,740
you don't see canes, you don't see walkers.

246
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:19,180
Wheelchairs are rare.

247
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:21,820
Most had never even heard the words joint replacement.

248
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:24,620
So I had to ask, how can joints use that heavily

249
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:28,220
day after day, stay pain-free for decades?

250
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:29,700
So we watched what they did.

251
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:31,540
Every evening, almost without exception,

252
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:34,380
they drank a warm preparation made from a golden root,

253
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:37,140
a root their culture has used for generations.

254
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:39,900
Back in the lab, we finally understood why.

255
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:42,260
It increases blood flow inside the joint.

256
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:45,020
You see blood is how the body repairs itself.

257
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:47,540
When you cut your skin, blood rushes to the area.

258
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:49,180
It carries repair cells with it.

259
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:51,380
And little by little, the tissue rebuilds.

260
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:54,140
The same repair process happens inside your joints.

261
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:56,620
This golden root drives nutrient-rich blood directly

262
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,780
in a damaged cartilage.

263
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:59,580
It allows your body to rebuild cartilage

264
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,980
and restore the slippery fluid that

265
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,620
keeps bones from grinding.

266
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:04,980
And that's what allows joints to move smoothly again

267
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:05,900
without pain.

268
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:07,740
But we discovered something critical.

269
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:10,580
You can't rebuild joint tissue while cadmium chloride

